@@s051 Your <code>Exercises.scala</code> of week 5, as it is now in the repo (I only read it and compiled it on a copy): Scala 3.8.4 stops with 4 errors.
@@s052 The variable is called <code>num</code>, not <code>i</code>: <code>else num</code>.
@@s053 In the same block a name is declared only once. The second value is an integer: call it <code>numInt</code> and return <code>((numDouble, numInt), rand2)</code>. The second error comes from the first: the pair contained two Doubles, the return type wanted (Double, Int).
@@s054 It is the <code>flatMap</code> of the LazyList of week 4, but here <code>f</code> is a generator, not a list: there is nothing to "fold". The solution is on the <a href="s05-rand.html">Rand page</a>.
